    "authorAssociation": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.surround\n\n### Question\n\ni'm not really sure what's wrong but since i've upgraded to v0.11 of neovim mini.surround's keybinds stopped waiting for my key chords as long as they used to and executing moderately complex surround commands (like `saiW]`) became much harder, unless i type all 6 strokes with perfect consistency and no pauses `mini.surround` just bails on me and does nothing",
    "bodyHTML": "<h3 dir=\"auto\">Contributing guidelines</h3>\n<ul class=\"contains-task-list\">\n<li class=\"task-list-item\"><input type=\"checkbox\" id=\"\" disabled=\"\" class=\"task-list-item-checkbox\" aria-label=\"Completed task\" checked=\"\"> I have read <a href=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\">CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md</a></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Module(s)</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">mini.surround</p>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Question</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">i'm not really sure what's wrong but since i've upgraded to v0.11 of neovim mini.surround's keybinds stopped waiting for my key chords as long as they used to and executing moderately complex surround commands (like <code class=\"notranslate\">saiW]</code>) became much harder, unless i type all 6 strokes with perfect consistency and no pauses <code class=\"notranslate\">mini.surround</code> just bails on me and does nothing</p>",
    "bodyText": "Contributing guidelines\n\n I have read CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md\n\nModule(s)\nmini.surround\nQuestion\ni'm not really sure what's wrong but since i've upgraded to v0.11 of neovim mini.surround's keybinds stopped waiting for my key chords as long as they used to and executing moderately complex surround commands (like saiW]) became much harder, unless i type all 6 strokes with perfect consistency and no pauses mini.surround just bails on me and does nothing",
